kind how-do-i
title How do I show one terminal on two displays?
intro A path can hold several displays. Every display in the path shows the same terminal, and the keyboard in the path types into it.
see heads-and-rules/show-a-terminal-on-a-display

file etc/vtium.conf
    version = 1
    font-name = unifont
    [head console]
    vt = 5
file etc/batch.conf
    ROOT/fonts/mono.bdf
font fonts/mono.bdf 8x16
device display HDMI-A-1 GSM:0x5b88:LEFT0001
device display DP-1 DEL:0xa0c1:RIGHT0001
device keyboard 046d:c31c USB Keyboard

1. Go to the Flow tab.
2. Highlight HDMI-A-1.
3. Press Space to pick.
4. Highlight DP-1.
5. Press Space to pick.
6. Highlight USB Keyboard.
7. Press Space to pick.
8. Press a to add path.
9. Press s to save.
at the save
check draft display HDMI-A-1 reaches terminal-1
check draft display DP-1 reaches terminal-1
check draft input USB Keyboard reaches terminal-1
